WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.892 --> 00:00:05.850
DINO CHIESA: Dino here.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.300
In this video, we're going
to cover Apigee tracing.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.030
If you haven't got a
working API proxy with API

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.450
key verification,
stop here and go back

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.550
and view the prior videos now.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.930
In the Apigee UI, select the
proxy we created previously.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:26.230
This proxy has the
verify API key policy.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.930
Let's use that to
learn about tracing.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.270
Select the Trace tab.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:33.610
Clicking this green
button tells Apigee

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.940
to begin collecting diagnostic
information for each request

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.640
it receives for the proxy.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.280
Let's invoke the API again
and we'll see how that works.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.380
I want to make sure I
pass a valid API key.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.690
In the trace window, you
can see, immediately,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:56.150
I have a trace record
for that request.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.460
Exploring here, I can
see the properties

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:03.105
of the inbound request and also
the results of the verify API

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:03.605
key policy.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.980
I can also see the
outbound request

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.390
being sent to the target.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:12.470
And what's this?

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:16.690
The API key is being
passed to the backend.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:19.410
That's because the Apigee
Edge proxy is passing

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.970
through the request unchanged.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.550
If we want to avoid that,
we can configure the proxy

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:29.840
to modify the request to
remove that query parameter.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:30.800
Let's do that.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:39.180
In the preflow, I'll add
an assign message policy.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.970
Assign message is a
multipurpose policy

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.310
that can be used to set or
change any part of a message.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.430
Normally, Apigee Edge
propagates an exact copy

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.760
of the inbound
message to the target.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.680
But with assign message,
you can make changes--

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.730
adding or removing
headers, adding or removing

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:01.910
query parameters.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:03.500
I'm going to
configure this policy

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.150
to remove the query parameter.

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.699
Save the proxy.

00:02:09.699 --> 00:02:11.800
Flip back to the trace tab.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.960
Start a trace session.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.390
Now invoke the API and
flip back to trace.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.030
And we can see the
assigned message policy is

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:26.800
removing the query parameter.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:30.190
The proxy is no longer leaking
that API key to the backend.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.230
Great.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:35.080
Apigee Edge trace gives
near real-time diagnostic

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.740
information to API proxy
developers during development.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.470
It will show you up
to 20 transactions.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:44.200
Now, it's not intended to
deliver a log of transactions.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.040
For that, you can use the
message logging policy.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.380
In this video, we used
the trace facility

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.960
and we tried the
assign message policy.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.990
That's just one of the
set of 30-plus policies

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:58.690
that are built into Apigee Edge.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.120
Don't forget, to learn
more, check out the product

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.160
documentation and
visit the community

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.070
site to explore further.

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.230
Be sure to watch the
next video in this series

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.260
where we'll cover the
API developer portal.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:13.000
Until next time,
keep it digital.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.350
[MUSIC PLAYING]

